{
  "startedAt": "2026-10-16T02:23:33.820Z",
  "steps": [
    "Existing World resource binding previews without writes, then saves exactly one audio metadata file. Source and both WAV files stay unchanged; this saved binding is separate from subsequent source editing.",
    "Both tracks choose the bound replacement WAV while retaining identities/cues. Chinese, English and Japanese at 390px retain selection and volume; Cancel leaves the source draft and author tree unchanged, including the separately saved metadata binding.",
    "Apply changes only the ordinary unsaved source draft. Ordinary Save updates exactly the reviewed audio JSON; metadata, scene, referenced WAV and other author files remain byte-identical.",
    "Saved audio reopens with both original track identities and cue bindings, the selected replacement resource and independent volumes. The old WAV remains in author assets and metadata.",
    "The same scene plans, builds and runs through real Godot. The host validates both original tracks and three original cue commands with the replacement resource: music play, effect play and music stop, with independent actor/audio completion.",
    "Chrome downloads the generated engine project ZIP. Independent verification confirms one deduplicated WAV resource, extraction preserves its exact bytes and settings, and fresh Godot import/run at another path produces identical audio events."
  ],
